WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.660
Picture two lamps.

2
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.380
One glows a bright, deep red.

3
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.680
The other gives out only a
faint, weak glow of ultraviolet.

4
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.020
Hours under the red light leave
the DNA in skin cells unharmed.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:16.120
A few minutes of the
ultraviolet can damage it.

6
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.160
How can the weaker light
do the greater damage?

7
00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:23.440
In this mission, you'll find out that
light is emitted and absorbed in tiny,

8
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.130
separate packets, called photons.

9
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.600
Then you'll measure their
energies in a tiny new unit:

10
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:35.220
the electronvolt, the energy an electron
gains when accelerated through 1 volt.

11
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:40.640
Your mission: explain why weak ultraviolet
can damage DNA when bright red light

12
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.400
can't.
